      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The square’s name means “new market” and dates back to the 13th‑century toll document that first mentioned the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amsterdam",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nieuwmarkt’s history is tied to the dam that controlled flooding at the mouth of the Amstel, built between 1264 and 1275.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amsterdam",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today the square borders Amsterdam’s historic Chinatown, a vibrant enclave that began flourishing in the late 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://wittetulp.nl/experience-nieuwmarkt-amsterdam-2024-historic-square-and-chinatown/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area once hosted a bustling market where merchants traded spices, textiles, and precious metals during the Golden Age.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [],
      "sourceLabels": [
